extraction of mantra|extraction of mantra\nSanskrit: mantroddhāra <Word/Term/Phrase>\n\n\nTibetan renderings of mantroddhāra: {sngags btu ba/}, {sngags btu ba/}\n\nTechnically, a mantroddhāra  consists in extracting the components of a mantra from the Sanskrit alphabet of fifty letters (the anusvāra, visarga, and ligature kṣa are considered independent elements). These components are encoded in special mnemonic phrases, usually in versified form. By decoding those often enigmatic verses, ‘devinettes’ to borrow André Padoux’s expression, the practitioner reconstructs the mantra.\nOccasionally, it is indicated as one of the ten fields of competence for a Tantric officiant of the Higher Tantras (daśatattva).\n\nSee the full entry at:https://www.itlr.net/hwid:109926
