non food|non-food, non-fuel\nSanskrit: anāhāra <Word/Term/Phrase>\n\n\nTibetan renderings of anāhāra: {zas ma yin pa/}\n\nThe technical term anāhāra designates those things, factors or meditation objects which (a) prevent the occurrence of one of the five hindrances (nivaraṇa) for meditation and successful soteriological practice or/and (b) serve as an antidote against a hindrance that has already arisen.\n\nSee the full entry at:https://www.itlr.net/hwid:157501
