in short|in short, briefly, succinctly\nSanskrit: samāsatas <Word/Term/Phrase>\n\n\nTibetan renderings of samāsatas: {mdor bsdu na/}\n\nind. in a summary manner, succinctly, concisely, Mn.; R.; VarBṛS. &c.\nExample: aparinirvāṇadharmakaḥ…samāsato dvividhaḥ / tatkālāparinirvāṇadharmā atyantaṃ ca / (yongs su mya ngan las mi ’da’ ba’i chos can…mdor bsdu na rnam pa gnyis te / de’i dus dang gtan yongs su mya ngan las mi ’da’ ba’i chos can no //).\nExample: tatra viśuddhiḥ samāsato dvividhā / prakṛtiviśuddhir vaimalyaviśuddhiś ca / (de la rnam par dag pa ni mdor bsdu na rnam pa gnyis te / rang bzhin gyis rnam par dag pa dang dri ma med pa’i rnam par dag pa’o //).\n\nSee the full entry at:https://www.itlr.net/hwid:53821
