Diamond Vehicle|Diamond Vehicle\nSanskrit: vajrayāna <Word/Term/Phrase>\n\n\nTibetan renderings of vajrayāna: {rdo rje theg pa/}, {rdo rje theg/}, {rdo rje'i theg pa/}\n\nvajrayāna, nt., a Tantric form of Mahāyāna: Sādh 225.10.\nThe earliest attestations of this headword in texts surviving in Sanskrit are probably those in the Sarvatathāgatatattvasaṃgraha, the fundamental Yogatantra scripture. Note that there it is always “this sūtra” (idaṃ sūtram) that is said to be (the) supreme (anuttara) Vajrayāna, and, be it noted, a compendium/epitome of the Mahāyāna (mahāyānābhisaṃgraha).\nSome of the primary sources for the occurrence of the term vajrayāna that have been identified by Francesco Sferra are: Laghukālacakratantra\n 3.2a, Vimalaprabhā II, p. 3 ff., Paramārthasevā stt. 3, 171, Ṣaḍaṅgayoga p. 94, Guṇabharaṇī p. 94,  Amṛtakaṇikā p. 4, Abhayapaddhati chapter 13 (where there is a contrast with the Pāramitānaya).\n\nSee the full entry at:https://www.itlr.net/hwid:11414
