impure substance|impure substance (or bodily component)\nSanskrit: aśucidravya <Word/Term/Phrase>\n\n\nTibetan renderings of aśucidravya: {mi gtsang ba'i rdzas/}\n\nIn Buddhist Sanskrit texts, lists of impure bodily substances are often given. Although most of the items are contained in each of these lists, variations occur on a regular basis as well. Often, these lists are accompanied by lists of external impure substances (in particular, lists of corpses in their various stages of decay).\nBelow, several lists of such aśucidravya-s are given, although the term itself does not occur in any of these passages. but note the use of aśuci in this sense in some of the occurrences. Very probably, aśubhatā as used in the Śrāvakabhūmi also has to be understood in this concrete collective sense.\n\nSee the full entry at:https://www.itlr.net/hwid:573885
