Result|Result/Fruit Vehicle\nSanskrit: phalayāna <Word/Term/Phrase>\n\n\nTibetan renderings of phalayāna: {'bras bu'i theg pa/}\n\nThe term phalayāna has been flagged (with an asterisk) as not yet attested in Kyuma 2009: 477. There are indeed no occurrences to be found, it seems, in Sanskrit texts that have been published up to now. The two cited from as yet unpublished works below date from no earlier than the eleventh century.\nThe idea of phalayāna may well have been inspired by the idea expressed in Mañjuśrīnāmasaṃgīti 135cd: yānatritayaniryāta ekayānaphale sthitaḥ /. Note that the second passage in “Occurrences in Primary Sources: Indic” below is from a commentary on exactly that hemistich.\n\nSee the full entry at:https://www.itlr.net/hwid:674055
